1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:29,980
We'll be right back.

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:59,980
We'll be right back.

3
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:04,220
Corey knows that I get a little bit nervous talking to you guys.

4
00:01:04,220 --> 00:01:09,660
You're a lot more intimidating than, you know, the kids I'm usually speaking with.

5
00:01:09,660 --> 00:01:12,020
But so he's my biggest fan this morning.

6
00:01:12,020 --> 00:01:12,360
Thanks, Corey.

7
00:01:12,360 --> 00:01:14,080
My name is Michelle Meeks.

8
00:01:14,080 --> 00:01:15,660
I'm the children's pastor here.

9
00:01:15,660 --> 00:01:20,480
So if I haven't met you, it's because I get to hang out with your kids, and I have a blast

10
00:01:20,480 --> 00:01:21,080
every Sunday.

11
00:01:21,480 --> 00:01:26,540
And I'm super excited to get to be with you as we continue the series, Go and Tell.

12
00:01:26,540 --> 00:01:32,840
We're on the third week where we are looking at how our church can seek to fulfill the Great

13
00:01:32,840 --> 00:01:37,440
Commission, the last commandment Jesus gave us before he ascended back into heaven.

14
00:01:37,440 --> 00:01:41,360
And so for the first two weeks, Ryan kind of gave you an overarching view.

15
00:01:41,360 --> 00:01:46,620
Our church values, our mission statement, and he explained that there are both internal and

16
00:01:46,620 --> 00:01:48,840
external components to the Great Commission.

17
00:01:48,840 --> 00:01:55,320
This morning, I get to talk to you about the internal components and how you can participate

18
00:01:55,320 --> 00:02:01,340
in our strategy to serve those within these walls together.

19
00:02:01,340 --> 00:02:03,020
So I have to be honest.

20
00:02:03,020 --> 00:02:08,100
This was a bit of a challenge for me because as I just stated, I'm the children's pastor here.

21
00:02:08,100 --> 00:02:10,460
We are blessed with so many kids.

22
00:02:10,580 --> 00:02:13,880
I was just kind of blown away for a second watching all the teenagers leave.

23
00:02:13,880 --> 00:02:16,020
For a minute, I thought you guys were all just leaving.

24
00:02:16,020 --> 00:02:22,220
But there was like 40 kids that just got up and left, which is amazing.

25
00:02:22,220 --> 00:02:26,140
So with that blessing comes a great need for volunteers.

26
00:02:26,140 --> 00:02:32,620
If we end up going to two services at Easter, then the need for volunteers goes up.

27
00:02:32,620 --> 00:02:39,700
So my conflict and my worry with this message is sometimes when you have a message about serving,

28
00:02:39,700 --> 00:02:44,380
you can kind of tend to like shut down and be like, oh gosh, not again.

29
00:02:44,380 --> 00:02:45,340
I am swamped.

30
00:02:45,340 --> 00:02:46,560
I have so many things going on.

31
00:02:46,560 --> 00:02:49,180
Please don't try to give me anything else to put on my plate.

32
00:02:49,180 --> 00:02:54,540
And I've seen the blessing that those that serve get.

33
00:02:54,540 --> 00:02:56,420
I've seen the blessing that the children get.

34
00:02:56,420 --> 00:03:02,420
And so my challenge for you is if you have that internal pool, if you're being honest with yourself,

35
00:03:02,420 --> 00:03:08,240
I would just like you, as the song said, to just give God a chance to speak to you.

36
00:03:08,240 --> 00:03:10,940
I promise no one's going to make you volunteer for anything.

37
00:03:10,940 --> 00:03:15,060
But he's taught me so much as I prepared this message.

38
00:03:15,060 --> 00:03:19,480
And so I don't want you to miss any of it if you have that pool.

39
00:03:19,480 --> 00:03:22,080
So let's just dive in.

40
00:03:22,660 --> 00:03:30,360
To begin with, I want to look at what the Bible says about you and I once we've made the decision to follow Christ.

41
00:03:30,360 --> 00:03:37,560
So once you've decided that Jesus is who he said he was and you want to follow him as the King of kings and Lord of his lords,

42
00:03:37,560 --> 00:03:40,360
what does the Bible say about you in that moment?

43
00:03:40,360 --> 00:03:44,860
If you look at Romans 1, 16, it says,

44
00:03:44,860 --> 00:03:52,540
For I am not ashamed of the gospel, because it is the power of God that brings salvation to everyone who believes.

45
00:03:53,080 --> 00:03:55,500
First to the Jew, then to the Gentile.

46
00:03:55,500 --> 00:04:00,620
If you've been around church for any amount of years or days, you've heard the word gospel, right?

47
00:04:00,620 --> 00:04:03,260
That's a word that gets thrown around all the time.

48
00:04:03,260 --> 00:04:05,760
And this says, For I am not ashamed of the gospel.

49
00:04:05,760 --> 00:04:10,200
So before we get ahead of ourselves, what does the word gospel actually mean?

50
00:04:10,360 --> 00:04:14,440
So the word gospel comes from the Greek word euangelion.

51
00:04:14,440 --> 00:04:17,140
If you know Greek, I apologize if I butchered that.

52
00:04:17,140 --> 00:04:19,400
But it means good news.

53
00:04:19,400 --> 00:04:29,920
In the New Testament, it refers to the announcement of the understanding that Jesus brought the reign of God to earth in his life, death, and resurrection.

54
00:04:30,200 --> 00:04:35,480
So when we're talking about the gospel, that's what we're talking about, the whole story that Jesus was the Messiah, and he came.

55
00:04:35,480 --> 00:04:39,400
He lived a life worthy for us to follow.

56
00:04:39,400 --> 00:04:42,880
He gave his life on the cross for you and I, and he rose again.

57
00:04:42,880 --> 00:04:44,040
That's the gospel.

58
00:04:45,660 --> 00:04:51,740
When you come to a place in your life that you have that understanding, it literally changes.

59
00:04:51,740 --> 00:04:54,840
When you've accepted that, it changes who you are.

60
00:04:54,840 --> 00:04:58,160
Look at 2 Corinthians 5.17.

61
00:04:58,160 --> 00:05:01,740
Therefore, if anyone is in Christ, he is a new creation.

62
00:05:01,740 --> 00:05:03,840
The old has passed away.

63
00:05:03,840 --> 00:05:05,680
The new has come.

64
00:05:05,680 --> 00:05:10,260
You are a new creation the moment you make that decision.

65
00:05:10,840 --> 00:05:13,980
You are now seen as blameless in God's eyes.

66
00:05:13,980 --> 00:05:21,380
Because of the atonement of Jesus on the cross, you are no longer seen by your faults, by your sins in the past, present, and future.

67
00:05:21,380 --> 00:05:25,220
You are seen as blameless in God's eyes, and you are a new creation.

68
00:05:25,220 --> 00:05:30,560
So this should be the most freeing thing to you once you make this step.

69
00:05:30,560 --> 00:05:32,360
It's nothing like the world offers, right?

70
00:05:32,360 --> 00:05:38,240
There is nothing on this earth that gives us this freedom.

71
00:05:38,680 --> 00:05:44,100
Everything we have here we have to earn, and Jesus is saying, you can't earn what I'm giving you.

72
00:05:44,100 --> 00:05:48,620
You are seen as blameless because of what I did on the cross for you.

73
00:05:48,620 --> 00:06:00,760
Nothing you can do can take that away or earn it, and so we should be so free and full of happiness for the fact that Jesus has given us that gift.

74
00:06:00,760 --> 00:06:05,100
But the gospel doesn't end there, or it shouldn't.

75
00:06:05,100 --> 00:06:15,520
The gospel should go deeper into you, changing you every day, every moment, as you learn more and more.

76
00:06:15,520 --> 00:06:19,800
As long as you are seeking God, he's going to continue to change you through the gospel.

77
00:06:19,800 --> 00:06:26,880
And the goal is that you should hopefully be able to see the world through the eyes of Jesus, no longer through your own eyes.

78
00:06:27,380 --> 00:06:33,340
So the Bible gives us a lot of examples of this, how people accept Christ, but then they begin to change.

79
00:06:33,340 --> 00:06:41,020
The gospel goes deeper into them, and you see them begin to change and form into a person who sees the world through Jesus' eyes.

80
00:06:41,020 --> 00:06:42,680
So I want to give you two quick examples.

81
00:06:42,680 --> 00:06:45,180
In Galatians 2, we have Paul and Peter.

82
00:06:45,600 --> 00:06:50,700
So Peter was one of Jesus' disciples, so he got to walk with Jesus for all three years of his ministry.

83
00:06:50,700 --> 00:06:52,140
He got to ask him questions.

84
00:06:52,140 --> 00:06:53,060
He saw the miracles.

85
00:06:53,060 --> 00:06:54,720
He watched him be crucified.

86
00:06:54,720 --> 00:06:56,320
He watched him come back to life.

87
00:06:56,320 --> 00:07:00,460
So you would think he would have a very good understanding of the gospel.

88
00:07:00,460 --> 00:07:02,740
He was there for a lot of it.

89
00:07:02,740 --> 00:07:03,740
And then you have Paul.

90
00:07:03,740 --> 00:07:06,620
Paul did not believe that Jesus was who he said he was.

91
00:07:06,620 --> 00:07:10,260
He has an encounter with Jesus on the road to Damascus, and his life changes.

92
00:07:10,260 --> 00:07:17,840
So you have these two men, and in this situation, Peter is still obeying Old Testament law.

93
00:07:17,840 --> 00:07:19,400
So he was a Jew by birth.

94
00:07:19,400 --> 00:07:23,580
Old Testament law says that Jews were not allowed to sit and eat with Gentiles.

95
00:07:23,580 --> 00:07:25,200
Gentiles were considered unclean.

96
00:07:25,200 --> 00:07:28,840
And so in this situation, Peter is not eating with Gentiles.

97
00:07:28,940 --> 00:07:35,180
He's kind of elevating himself above the Gentiles, and Paul sees this, and he knows that it's

98
00:07:35,180 --> 00:07:35,600
not right.

99
00:07:35,600 --> 00:07:40,840
He knows that Peter knows this, but the gospel hadn't gone deep enough into him that's made

100
00:07:40,840 --> 00:07:41,600
him change.

101
00:07:41,600 --> 00:07:44,260
So Paul lovingly confronts him.

102
00:07:44,260 --> 00:07:49,980
Galatians 2, 14 through 16, when I saw that they were not following the truth of the gospel

103
00:07:49,980 --> 00:07:55,160
message, I said to Peter in front of the others, since you, a Jew by birth, have discarded

104
00:07:55,160 --> 00:08:01,340
the Jewish law, and are living like a Gentile, why are you now trying to make these Gentiles

105
00:08:01,340 --> 00:08:02,720
follow Jewish traditions?

106
00:08:02,720 --> 00:08:08,780
You and I are Jews by birth, not sinners, quotation marks, like the Gentiles.

107
00:08:08,780 --> 00:08:15,260
Yet we know that a person is made right with God by faith in Jesus Christ, not by obeying

108
00:08:15,260 --> 00:08:15,740
the law.

109
00:08:15,740 --> 00:08:20,700
Peter knew this, but the truth hadn't gone deep enough into him.

110
00:08:20,700 --> 00:08:24,500
There was still a lot of transforming that his heart needed to do.

111
00:08:24,500 --> 00:08:28,700
Paul saw this, and he's helping him to grow closer to Jesus.

112
00:08:28,700 --> 00:08:37,180
This is ministry, coming alongside of someone and lovingly reminding them, neither of us deserve

113
00:08:37,180 --> 00:08:37,520
this.

114
00:08:37,520 --> 00:08:39,560
Paul and Peter, we were there for the whole way.

115
00:08:39,560 --> 00:08:40,140
We were there.

116
00:08:40,140 --> 00:08:40,880
We knew Jesus.

117
00:08:40,880 --> 00:08:41,700
Well, Peter did.

118
00:08:41,700 --> 00:08:43,640
But we don't deserve the salvation.

119
00:08:43,640 --> 00:08:45,100
The Gentiles don't.

120
00:08:45,100 --> 00:08:45,840
The Jews don't.

121
00:08:45,840 --> 00:08:51,760
But we were both accepted into his family because of the atonement Jesus made.

122
00:08:51,760 --> 00:08:53,420
Let me give you another example.

123
00:08:53,840 --> 00:08:55,280
James 1, 9 through 10.

124
00:08:55,280 --> 00:09:04,820
James is giving people who are both rich in monetary amounts and poor a different way

125
00:09:04,820 --> 00:09:05,780
to look at the gospel.

126
00:09:05,780 --> 00:09:13,400
So he says in verses 9 and 10, believers who are poor have something to boast about, for

127
00:09:13,400 --> 00:09:14,540
God has honored them.

128
00:09:14,540 --> 00:09:18,400
And those who are rich should boast that God has humbled them.

129
00:09:18,980 --> 00:09:20,080
So what is this?

130
00:09:20,080 --> 00:09:21,960
He's talking about the gospel.

131
00:09:21,960 --> 00:09:29,280
He's saying if you are poor and society looks down on you, if you are constantly doubting

132
00:09:29,280 --> 00:09:31,320
yourself, you need to look at the gospel.

133
00:09:31,320 --> 00:09:37,720
The gospel tells you that God has elevated you and you are welcome into the kingdom of heaven.

134
00:09:37,960 --> 00:09:43,780
If you are rich and society is constantly telling you how amazing you are, you need to look at

135
00:09:43,780 --> 00:09:44,280
the gospel.

136
00:09:44,280 --> 00:09:48,720
You need to be reminded that you don't deserve the salvation that you've been given.

137
00:09:48,720 --> 00:09:51,000
And knock yourself down a couple pegs.

138
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:56,220
Look at the gospel and be reminded of who you are in Christ because that's what matters.

139
00:09:56,220 --> 00:09:58,520
Who we are in the world doesn't matter.

140
00:09:58,520 --> 00:10:00,340
Who we are in Christ is all that matters.

141
00:10:00,440 --> 00:10:05,960
So he's just reminding us, never forget who you are in Christ.

142
00:10:05,960 --> 00:10:07,700
Think about it this way.

143
00:10:07,700 --> 00:10:12,300
If you believe you're worthless, you won't be able to see how highly God views you.

144
00:10:12,300 --> 00:10:18,420
On the other hand, if you are always being told how wonderful you are, you can become arrogant

145
00:10:18,420 --> 00:10:23,340
and get caught up in what the world offers and miss what God is showing you.

146
00:10:23,340 --> 00:10:29,280
James is challenging the believer to rise above what the world tells you you are.

147
00:10:29,940 --> 00:10:37,340
Do you view yourself, if you're honest, based on how the world views you or how Jesus views

148
00:10:37,340 --> 00:10:37,580
you?

149
00:10:37,580 --> 00:10:44,440
James is challenging us to constantly look at ourselves through Jesus' eyes, not through

150
00:10:44,440 --> 00:10:44,860
the world.

151
00:10:44,860 --> 00:10:46,580
This is ministry.

152
00:10:46,580 --> 00:10:50,640
It's taking the gospel deeper, not allowing it to be surface level.

153
00:10:50,640 --> 00:10:55,140
Yes, when you become a Christian, you are seen as blameless, but he doesn't want you to

154
00:10:55,140 --> 00:11:00,600
walk on this earth and just sit with that and not go deeper.

155
00:11:00,600 --> 00:11:07,420
There are so many levels to the gospel and the longer I spend with Jesus, the more I realize

156
00:11:07,420 --> 00:11:09,640
there's so much more that I have to learn.

157
00:11:09,640 --> 00:11:14,540
But each time he teaches me something, I grow deeper in him.

158
00:11:14,540 --> 00:11:15,540
I bless him more.

159
00:11:15,540 --> 00:11:20,400
I begin to see things through Jesus' eyes more than my own eyes, and it's an incredible

160
00:11:20,400 --> 00:11:23,780
thing, yet I have so much more to go.

161
00:11:23,780 --> 00:11:30,320
A good friend of mine, Dave Ballinger, I think he's actually with the kids right now.

162
00:11:30,320 --> 00:11:36,360
So he once told me something a few years ago when we were going, he's like, he's an incredible

163
00:11:36,360 --> 00:11:36,620
guy.

164
00:11:36,620 --> 00:11:38,320
If you don't know him, you should get to know him.

165
00:11:38,320 --> 00:11:38,760
He's amazing.

166
00:11:38,840 --> 00:11:41,360
But he once told me something that I've never forgotten.

167
00:11:41,360 --> 00:11:46,480
He said, the closer I get to God, the more I realize how far away from him I was.

168
00:11:46,480 --> 00:11:48,280
And that is so true.

169
00:11:48,280 --> 00:11:50,540
The closer you get, the more you find out about him.

170
00:11:50,540 --> 00:11:56,460
The more that you see him move, which I get to see daily working with your kids, the closer

171
00:11:56,460 --> 00:11:58,100
you get and the more you trust him.

172
00:11:58,100 --> 00:12:03,920
The things of this world don't rock you as much as they used to because you see God in

173
00:12:03,920 --> 00:12:04,460
everything.

174
00:12:04,460 --> 00:12:11,400
Romans 12, 2 says, do not conform to the patterns of this world, but be transformed by

175
00:12:11,400 --> 00:12:12,580
the renewing of your mind.

176
00:12:12,580 --> 00:12:16,200
He is literally renewing our minds.

177
00:12:16,200 --> 00:12:21,060
So keeping all of this in mind, the fact that you're a new creation the moment you accept

178
00:12:21,060 --> 00:12:27,180
Christ as your Lord and Savior, but that your mind is being daily removed and that the gospel

179
00:12:27,180 --> 00:12:31,680
must go deeper into you in order for you to be more like Christ, I'd like to look at another

180
00:12:31,680 --> 00:12:33,940
Scripture that comes right before Romans 12, 2.

181
00:12:33,940 --> 00:12:42,640
Romans 12, 1 says, therefore I urge you, brothers and sisters, in view of God's mercy to offer

182
00:12:42,640 --> 00:12:47,720
your bodies as a living sacrifice, holy and pleasing to God.

183
00:12:47,720 --> 00:12:49,680
This is your spiritual act of worship.

184
00:12:49,680 --> 00:12:55,380
So because of the gospel, because you have a deep understanding of who God is, because he

185
00:12:55,380 --> 00:12:59,260
is transforming your mind, you are called to be a living sacrifice.

186
00:12:59,260 --> 00:13:02,860
If you've been around church for a while, you've heard this Scripture.

187
00:13:02,860 --> 00:13:08,000
But the question is, what does a living sacrifice actually mean?

188
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:10,840
It's a lot weirder than you think it is.

189
00:13:10,840 --> 00:13:17,580
The word sacrifice is actually the Greek word for killing.

190
00:13:17,580 --> 00:13:21,080
So you are called to be a living killing.

191
00:13:22,120 --> 00:13:23,960
It's deliberately paradoxical.

192
00:13:23,960 --> 00:13:30,080
The more I read the Bible, this is one of the many things God has taught me since having

193
00:13:30,080 --> 00:13:34,980
this job, is you have to look at who the original audience of the Scripture was.

194
00:13:34,980 --> 00:13:40,460
I've heard it said that the Bible was not written to us, but for us.

195
00:13:40,460 --> 00:13:44,780
So who is the original author, or who is the original audience of this?

196
00:13:45,200 --> 00:13:49,080
So Paul is writing this, he's writing this to the Christian church in Rome.

197
00:13:49,080 --> 00:13:50,860
It's full of Jews and Gentiles.

198
00:13:50,860 --> 00:13:54,320
Christian church had just begun to expand.

199
00:13:54,320 --> 00:13:56,900
People were realizing that Jesus was the Messiah.

200
00:13:56,900 --> 00:14:03,120
But during this time, everyone, regardless if you were Jewish or not, would understand the

201
00:14:03,120 --> 00:14:03,940
role of a sacrifice.

202
00:14:03,940 --> 00:14:08,620
Many religions at that time understood that there was a deity and there were humans, and

203
00:14:08,620 --> 00:14:09,900
that we were on different levels.

204
00:14:09,900 --> 00:14:16,940
So to make yourself presentable to the deity, whether it was the real God or a false God,

205
00:14:16,940 --> 00:14:19,040
you had to perform some sort of sacrifice.

206
00:14:19,040 --> 00:14:24,660
In the Jewish law, it was an animal sacrifice to atone for your sin, but other religions had

207
00:14:24,660 --> 00:14:25,580
sacrifices too.

208
00:14:25,580 --> 00:14:31,500
So when he uses this word, living sacrifice, that generation would understand at least the

209
00:14:31,500 --> 00:14:32,400
sacrifice part.

210
00:14:32,400 --> 00:14:38,600
There were also temples around that people understood that's where you went to make,

211
00:14:38,620 --> 00:14:39,580
the sacrifices.

212
00:14:39,580 --> 00:14:44,300
Paul is talking to Christians at that time, and he's reminding them that the Christian

213
00:14:44,300 --> 00:14:51,060
life, the life that you're choosing, is both like and unlike the Old Testament sacrifice.

214
00:14:51,060 --> 00:14:54,360
First, let's look at two ways that it's different.

215
00:14:54,360 --> 00:15:00,440
First off, the Old Testament sacrifices, when you would bring an animal to be sacrificed, that

216
00:15:00,440 --> 00:15:01,600
was bloody, right?

217
00:15:01,600 --> 00:15:03,160
That was on purpose.

218
00:15:03,160 --> 00:15:08,600
Blood symbolized the life of the animal, representing the idea that without the shedding of blood,

219
00:15:08,620 --> 00:15:10,300
there is no forgiveness of sin.

220
00:15:10,300 --> 00:15:16,080
So essentially, the animal acted as a sacrifice for the sinner's life.

221
00:15:16,080 --> 00:15:22,820
The animal's blood allowed for atonement and reconciliation with God through that offering.

222
00:15:23,540 --> 00:15:28,620
This is not the way it is now, or it was when Paul was talking.

223
00:15:28,620 --> 00:15:30,740
There was no atoning for sin.

224
00:15:30,740 --> 00:15:34,560
The sacrifice he's talking about is not an atoning for sin.

225
00:15:34,560 --> 00:15:37,920
You do not offer a sacrifice to be forgiven.

226
00:15:37,920 --> 00:15:42,220
You don't say, I'm going to work really hard, I'm going to do all these great things, and

227
00:15:42,220 --> 00:15:45,420
then you're going to forgive me, and then I'll be right with God.

228
00:15:45,420 --> 00:15:47,220
That's not how it is now.

229
00:15:48,220 --> 00:15:55,420
Jesus' sacrifice on the cross ends all guilt offerings and sin offerings, as his death was

230
00:15:55,420 --> 00:15:56,800
the atonement for our sins.

231
00:15:56,800 --> 00:16:02,020
So this living sacrifice that they're talking about is different.

232
00:16:02,020 --> 00:16:09,520
A living sacrifice isn't a sacrifice to be forgiven, but an offering of gratitude and praise.

