456
00:31:17,180 --> 00:31:24,540
And the only reason that you get to know about it is because you answer the calling that God has placed on your life, and then he uses you.

457
00:31:24,540 --> 00:31:27,080
And then your relationship with him grows deeper.

458
00:31:27,080 --> 00:31:37,780
Because when you realize, you put that book in my heart for this man, and when that man realizes, you love me enough to put that book in his heart, everything changes.

459
00:31:38,140 --> 00:31:42,100
But it won't happen if we don't answer the calling that God has given us.

460
00:31:42,100 --> 00:31:50,700
If you're here thinking this isn't for you, that you aren't qualified, and that you're too busy, you aren't gifted, I want to close with a final thought.

461
00:31:50,700 --> 00:31:52,920
Look at 1 Peter 2.

462
00:31:52,980 --> 00:31:56,660
You are coming to Christ, who is the living cornerstone of God's temple.

463
00:31:56,660 --> 00:32:00,740
He was rejected by people, but he was chosen by God for a great honor.

464
00:32:00,740 --> 00:32:05,280
And you are living stones that God is building into his spiritual temple.

465
00:32:05,280 --> 00:32:09,060
So back in those days, again, who is the audience?

466
00:32:10,500 --> 00:32:12,380
Structures were made with a cornerstone.

467
00:32:12,380 --> 00:32:14,220
That's what started the building.

468
00:32:14,220 --> 00:32:15,400
You laid the cornerstone.

469
00:32:15,400 --> 00:32:16,380
It was the biggest stone.

470
00:32:16,380 --> 00:32:18,620
The weight of the building sat on that stone.

471
00:32:18,620 --> 00:32:21,220
It gave you the direction, the angles.

472
00:32:21,220 --> 00:32:25,980
And Peter is referring to Jesus as this cornerstone in our lives.

473
00:32:25,980 --> 00:32:27,260
Put him first.

474
00:32:27,260 --> 00:32:29,660
Allow the weight of the building to rest on him.

475
00:32:29,660 --> 00:32:32,620
Point your life in the directions that he gives you.

476
00:32:33,160 --> 00:32:40,960
But then, he goes on to say that you and I are living cornerstones that God is using to build his temple.

477
00:32:40,960 --> 00:32:46,660
So, you have Peter, again, one of the 12 disciples.

478
00:32:46,660 --> 00:32:48,400
He lived with, he walked with Jesus.

479
00:32:48,400 --> 00:32:49,860
He saw what Jesus had to offer.

480
00:32:49,860 --> 00:32:56,660
And Jesus actually refers to Peter as the stone at which he will build his church on.

481
00:32:58,560 --> 00:33:06,500
But, when it came time for crucifixion, when Jesus was suffering the most he's ever suffered before,

482
00:33:06,500 --> 00:33:13,200
Peter, his close friend, the one that was there with him through everything, denied him, not one time, but three times.

483
00:33:13,200 --> 00:33:17,160
When the whole world has turned their back on Jesus, Peter denied him.

484
00:33:17,160 --> 00:33:22,840
Fast forward to a couple days later, after Jesus has come back from the dead,

485
00:33:22,840 --> 00:33:25,020
Jesus is sitting with Peter on the beach.

486
00:33:25,020 --> 00:33:28,220
He says to Peter, do you love me?

487
00:33:28,300 --> 00:33:29,760
He's not condemning him.

488
00:33:29,760 --> 00:33:31,200
He's not making him feel bad.

489
00:33:31,200 --> 00:33:32,380
He just says, do you love me?

490
00:33:32,380 --> 00:33:35,140
And Peter says, yes, three times.

491
00:33:35,140 --> 00:33:37,680
And he says, feed my sheep.

492
00:33:37,680 --> 00:33:40,800
Peter had to have been thinking, Lord, are you nuts?

493
00:33:40,800 --> 00:33:43,260
I just failed you.

494
00:33:43,260 --> 00:33:44,180
I'm not a rock.

495
00:33:44,180 --> 00:33:45,040
I'm quicksand.

496
00:33:45,040 --> 00:33:48,480
Nothing about who I am deserves to be a ministry leader.

497
00:33:48,480 --> 00:33:53,560
You said I was the rock, and I immediately failed you with time, when the time came.

498
00:33:54,960 --> 00:34:02,220
And Jesus is saying, Peter, nothing makes you a better leader.

499
00:34:02,220 --> 00:34:10,220
Nothing makes you better at changing people's lives in Jesus' name than when your failure is plunged into his grace.

500
00:34:10,900 --> 00:34:15,680
See, the more failures you have, the more you realize the gospel's healing power.

501
00:34:15,680 --> 00:34:21,400
When I was preparing for this message, I 100% felt like, Peter, I can't do this.

502
00:34:21,400 --> 00:34:23,780
I am not worthy to be up there.

503
00:34:23,780 --> 00:34:25,520
And Jesus gave me this.

504
00:34:25,520 --> 00:34:33,260
The more failure you have, your failure plunged into my grace is what makes me able to use you.

505
00:34:33,640 --> 00:34:37,280
So if you're here thinking, I failed too many times, perfect.

506
00:34:37,280 --> 00:34:40,080
You know what forgiveness looks like.

507
00:34:40,080 --> 00:34:44,860
You know what it means like to not deserve the gift that you've been given.

508
00:34:44,860 --> 00:34:45,900
And none of us do.

509
00:34:45,900 --> 00:34:55,220
But the more you realize it, the more you're able to love Jesus into people's lives, to forgive, to welcome them into our church with no baggage.

510
00:34:55,220 --> 00:34:58,260
Because you know you don't deserve to be here either.

511
00:34:58,260 --> 00:35:00,920
And Jesus will use that.

512
00:35:00,920 --> 00:35:04,060
Many of you don't know how I became the children's pastor.

513
00:35:04,060 --> 00:35:06,380
My husband and I had just moved to Winchester.

514
00:35:06,380 --> 00:35:08,500
We had been searching for a church for a few years.

515
00:35:08,500 --> 00:35:13,620
And my kids just, no matter what church we went to, there's nothing wrong with the churches.

516
00:35:13,620 --> 00:35:14,160
They were great.

517
00:35:14,160 --> 00:35:15,720
My kids just didn't want to go.

518
00:35:15,720 --> 00:35:17,100
And they would cry.

519
00:35:17,100 --> 00:35:18,600
And they would get called out.

520
00:35:18,600 --> 00:35:19,440
And they'd sit with us.

521
00:35:19,440 --> 00:35:20,420
And you know that doesn't work.

522
00:35:20,720 --> 00:35:26,880
And so, one Sunday, we were sitting at Canvas Church, and the pastor announced they were looking for a children's pastor.

523
00:35:26,880 --> 00:35:28,520
And I got that nudge.

524
00:35:28,520 --> 00:35:32,240
You know the God nudge when you're like, what about you?

525
00:35:32,240 --> 00:35:37,000
I'm like, I didn't have any formal Bible training.

526
00:35:37,000 --> 00:35:38,940
I didn't go to school to be a children's pastor.

527
00:35:38,940 --> 00:35:40,200
I don't know how to run volunteers.

528
00:35:40,200 --> 00:35:40,660
Like, I don't.

529
00:35:40,660 --> 00:35:42,880
But he just kept nudging me.

530
00:35:42,880 --> 00:35:49,800
So within a month, I had resigned from my job, and I was on staff at a church having no idea what I was doing.

531
00:35:49,800 --> 00:35:55,120
But I have gotten to see God move in my life in ways that I can't imagine.

532
00:35:55,120 --> 00:35:58,420
I've seen volunteers become friends and family members.

533
00:35:58,420 --> 00:36:03,800
I've seen children find Jesus because a volunteer had the patience for them.

534
00:36:03,800 --> 00:36:10,500
And I would never give up anything that God has given me through following that.

535
00:36:10,500 --> 00:36:16,900
Imagine what God could do through you if you stepped out of your comfort zone and into your calling.

536
00:36:17,740 --> 00:36:24,980
How might God use you to point young children towards Jesus in a culture that is so stacked against them?

537
00:36:24,980 --> 00:36:32,620
How might God use your friendly presence to calm the fears of a recovering addict stepping into a church the first time?

538
00:36:32,620 --> 00:36:40,120
How might God use your hospitality to give lonely people a safe community to experience God's love?

539
00:36:40,200 --> 00:36:46,820
How might God use your service to bring the service to someone who's elderly and can't make it into the building?

540
00:36:46,820 --> 00:36:51,820
There are so many ways that God has gifted you specifically.

541
00:36:51,820 --> 00:36:55,720
And someone out there needs your gift.

542
00:36:55,720 --> 00:37:00,900
They will only find Jesus if you step out of your comfort zone and into his calling.

543
00:37:01,320 --> 00:37:09,980
Because what you've gone through is exactly what they need to hear to understand that they are welcome here and that God loves them and that they can't earn it.

544
00:37:09,980 --> 00:37:12,680
So it doesn't matter how many times they've messed up.

545
00:37:12,680 --> 00:37:17,300
There's always another chance to come back to Jesus, to crawl on that altar.

546
00:37:17,300 --> 00:37:19,140
He won't force you.

547
00:37:19,140 --> 00:37:22,060
He doesn't force anybody to crawl on any altar.

548
00:37:22,560 --> 00:37:25,440
But a living sacrifice leads to life.

549
00:37:25,440 --> 00:37:27,340
And he wants to give you that.

550
00:37:27,340 --> 00:37:32,720
I want to leave you with the words of a woman named Mrs. J.K. Barney.

551
00:37:32,720 --> 00:37:36,500
She lived in 1918 and she wanted to be a missionary.

552
00:37:36,500 --> 00:37:38,260
But she was a woman in 1918.

553
00:37:38,260 --> 00:37:39,980
She wasn't able to be a missionary.

554
00:37:39,980 --> 00:37:43,720
But God kept tugging at her heart in little ways.

555
00:37:43,720 --> 00:37:45,740
So there was this older gentleman and he was dying.

556
00:37:45,740 --> 00:37:48,840
And he was known through the community as being someone that was really mean.

557
00:37:49,300 --> 00:37:52,940
So people were sending food outside of his door, but they were leaving alone.

558
00:37:52,940 --> 00:37:55,180
So he was dying alone.

559
00:37:55,180 --> 00:37:56,780
So God tugged at her heart.

560
00:37:56,780 --> 00:37:58,440
She got that little God nudge.

561
00:37:58,440 --> 00:38:00,900
And he said, I want you to go up there.

562
00:38:00,900 --> 00:38:01,980
So she does.

563
00:38:01,980 --> 00:38:03,060
She answers the calling.

564
00:38:03,060 --> 00:38:04,780
And he's really mean to her.

565
00:38:04,780 --> 00:38:05,620
He's nasty.

566
00:38:05,620 --> 00:38:07,000
Tells her to get out of his house.

567
00:38:07,000 --> 00:38:08,820
And she leaves feeling defeated.

568
00:38:08,820 --> 00:38:10,980
All right, God, I did what you asked me to do.

569
00:38:10,980 --> 00:38:12,520
Clearly it didn't work.

570
00:38:12,520 --> 00:38:13,820
But I'm done.

571
00:38:13,820 --> 00:38:16,560
But he keeps tugging at her heart.

572
00:38:16,560 --> 00:38:18,220
She keeps getting this little tug.

573
00:38:18,540 --> 00:38:24,500
So finally, she realizes that she never fully gave him over to God.

574
00:38:24,500 --> 00:38:31,500
So she prays, oh, Christ, give me a little glimpse of the worth of a human soul.

575
00:38:31,500 --> 00:38:36,680
Then she stops and she asks the reader, have you ever prayed that prayer and meant it?

576
00:38:36,680 --> 00:38:38,600
Don't, she said.

577
00:38:38,600 --> 00:38:42,940
Unless you are willing to give up the ease and selfish pleasures,

578
00:38:42,940 --> 00:38:47,780
for life will be a different thing for you after he reveals it to you.

579
00:38:47,780 --> 00:38:51,900
So God answers her prayer and she gets this fire under her.

580
00:38:51,900 --> 00:38:53,960
And she's like, I don't care how he treats me.

581
00:38:53,960 --> 00:38:57,000
I am going up there because Jesus loved him.

582
00:38:57,000 --> 00:39:01,300
And so she goes back and he's mean to her again.

583
00:39:01,300 --> 00:39:04,780
She says, I don't know what I expected.

584
00:39:04,780 --> 00:39:08,340
But the man greeted me with an awful oath.

585
00:39:08,340 --> 00:39:09,560
Again, it's 1918.

586
00:39:09,560 --> 00:39:10,300
He was mean.

587
00:39:10,860 --> 00:39:13,640
But it didn't hurt as bad as it did before.

588
00:39:13,640 --> 00:39:16,720
And this was the line that just had me in tears.

589
00:39:16,720 --> 00:39:20,440
For I was behind Christ and I stayed there.

590
00:39:20,440 --> 00:39:23,880
You are not in this alone.

591
00:39:23,880 --> 00:39:27,740
We are not meant to go out there alone.

592
00:39:27,740 --> 00:39:33,960
We are meant to be behind Christ and stay there and let him lead us.

593
00:39:34,020 --> 00:39:39,280
Because there is nothing we can't handle if Christ is in front of us.

594
00:39:39,280 --> 00:39:44,380
God never intended for us to do this alone.

595
00:39:44,380 --> 00:39:47,800
But he has a calling specifically for you.

596
00:39:47,800 --> 00:39:49,700
It's not a top-down approach.

597
00:39:49,700 --> 00:39:52,660
God never intended it to be a top-down approach.

598
00:39:53,200 --> 00:39:54,620
Jesus bridged the gap.

599
00:39:54,620 --> 00:40:01,500
So now, what is it in your life that you have lived through that God wants to use?

600
00:40:01,500 --> 00:40:04,480
Just like Peter, we're not rocks.

601
00:40:04,480 --> 00:40:05,740
We are quicksand.

602
00:40:05,740 --> 00:40:11,500
But in Christ, with him in front and us behind, he can do incredible things.

603
00:40:11,500 --> 00:40:12,780
Let's pray.

604
00:40:12,780 --> 00:40:17,780
Dear Heavenly Father, I thank you for the words that you've given me, God.

605
00:40:17,780 --> 00:40:20,260
I pray for every person in this room.

606
00:40:20,260 --> 00:40:23,020
We have so much telling us we're not good enough.

607
00:40:23,200 --> 00:40:24,580
That we don't qualify.

608
00:40:24,580 --> 00:40:27,600
That we aren't the one you want to use.

609
00:40:27,600 --> 00:40:34,400
But I know from firsthand experience that you can take someone that has no right to be used and use them in ways they can never imagine.

610
00:40:34,400 --> 00:40:40,360
So I pray, whatever you're tugging on each heart here, God, that you would make it abundantly clear.

611
00:40:40,360 --> 00:40:42,900
Don't let us walk away.

612
00:40:42,900 --> 00:40:49,340
Keep tugging on our hearts until we get to witness your hand in our lives.

613
00:40:49,340 --> 00:40:53,380
Allow our church to walk into the roles that you've given us.

614
00:40:53,380 --> 00:40:54,960
I thank you for the experiences.

615
00:40:54,960 --> 00:40:59,700
I thank you for the fact that you have welcomed us into your family with open arms.

616
00:40:59,700 --> 00:41:01,040
We love you.

617
00:41:01,040 --> 00:41:01,960
In Jesus' name I pray.

618
00:41:01,960 --> 00:41:02,380
Amen.

619
00:41:02,380 --> 00:41:03,940
Thank you.

620
00:41:07,440 --> 00:41:08,240
Brian's coming up.

621
00:41:08,240 --> 00:41:08,640
Don't leave.

622
00:41:08,640 --> 00:41:10,800
Are you coming up?

623
00:41:10,800 --> 00:41:30,540
Y'all want to sing a chorus of Cornerstone?

624
00:41:32,720 --> 00:41:33,600
All right, let's stand.

625
00:41:33,600 --> 00:41:33,720
All right.

626
00:41:33,720 --> 00:41:35,720
Let's stand.

627
00:42:02,720 --> 00:42:32,700
Lord of all Christ alone.

628
00:42:32,720 --> 00:42:47,420
Cornerstone, weak made strong in the Savior's love and through the song.

629
00:42:47,420 --> 00:42:56,280
He is Lord, Lord of all.

630
00:42:56,280 --> 00:43:09,420
After that passage in Romans 12, Paul kind of gives a long description of what a church filled

631
00:43:09,420 --> 00:43:12,360
with people who function as living sacrifices looks like.

632
00:43:12,360 --> 00:43:16,120
And I just want to end our service today reading this over us as a prayer.

633
00:43:16,120 --> 00:43:20,780
May this be a description of what our church becomes as each and every single one of us live

634
00:43:20,780 --> 00:43:21,620
into our calling.

635
00:43:21,620 --> 00:43:26,620
To be like prophets who take God's word to the people in need.

636
00:43:26,620 --> 00:43:32,620
Like priests who represent people's needs before God and like ambassadors to King Jesus.

637
00:43:32,620 --> 00:43:34,020
It says this.

638
00:43:34,240 --> 00:43:37,680
Because of the privilege and authority God has given me, I give each of you this warning.

639
00:43:37,680 --> 00:43:39,960
Do not think of yourselves better than you really are.

640
00:43:39,960 --> 00:43:45,500
Be honest in your evaluation of yourselves, measuring yourselves by the faith that God has given you.

641
00:43:45,500 --> 00:43:51,300
Just as our bodies have many parts and each part has a special function, so it is with Christ's body.

642
00:43:51,400 --> 00:43:56,580
We each are many parts of one body and we all belong to each other.

643
00:43:56,580 --> 00:44:01,080
In his grace, he has given us different gifts for doing certain things well.

644
00:44:01,080 --> 00:44:06,260
So if God has given you the ability to speak, speak with as much faith as God has given you.

645
00:44:06,260 --> 00:44:08,920
And your gifts in serving others, serve them well.

646
00:44:08,920 --> 00:44:10,380
If you're a teacher, teach well.

647
00:44:10,380 --> 00:44:13,660
Or if you have the gift of encouragement, encourage others.

648
00:44:13,660 --> 00:44:16,400
If it is by giving, give generously.

649
00:44:16,940 --> 00:44:21,400
If God has given you leadership ability, take that responsibility seriously.

650
00:44:21,400 --> 00:44:25,480
And if you have a gift for showing kindness to others, do it gladly.

651
00:44:25,480 --> 00:44:28,280
Don't just pretend to love others, but really love them.

652
00:44:28,280 --> 00:44:29,900
Hate what is wrong.

653
00:44:29,900 --> 00:44:31,240
Hold tightly to what is good.

654
00:44:31,240 --> 00:44:36,700
Love each other with genuine affection and take delight in honoring one another.

655
00:44:36,700 --> 00:44:41,120
Never be lazy, but work hard and serve the Lord enthusiastically.

656
00:44:41,120 --> 00:44:43,380
Rejoice in confident hope.

657
00:44:43,380 --> 00:44:46,120
Be patient in trouble and keep on praying.

658
00:44:46,620 --> 00:44:52,280
When God's people are in need, be ready to help them and always be eager to practice hospitality.

659
00:44:52,280 --> 00:44:54,900
This is where it gets hard.

660
00:44:54,900 --> 00:44:57,440
Bless those who persecute you.

661
00:44:57,440 --> 00:44:58,320
Don't curse them.

662
00:44:58,320 --> 00:45:00,640
Pray that God will bless them.

663
00:45:00,640 --> 00:45:04,380
Be happy with those who are happy and weep with those who weep.

664
00:45:04,380 --> 00:45:05,780
Live in harmony with each other.

665
00:45:05,780 --> 00:45:10,400
Don't be too proud to enjoy the company of ordinary people and don't think you know it all.

666
00:45:10,400 --> 00:45:14,200
Never pay back evil with more evil.

667
00:45:14,960 --> 00:45:18,000
Do things in such a way that everyone can see you are honorable.

668
00:45:18,000 --> 00:45:20,940
Do all that you can to live at peace with everyone.

669
00:45:20,940 --> 00:45:28,880
Do all that you can to live at peace with everyone.

670
00:45:28,880 --> 00:45:33,040
Dear friends, never take revenge.

671
00:45:33,040 --> 00:45:37,800
Leave that to the righteous anger of God for the Scripture says, I will take revenge.

672
00:45:37,900 --> 00:45:39,460
I will pay them back says the Lord.

673
00:45:39,460 --> 00:45:41,620
Instead, if your enemies are hungry, feed them.

674
00:45:41,620 --> 00:45:44,260
If they are thirsty, give them something to drink.

675
00:45:44,260 --> 00:45:47,900
In doing this, you will heat burning coals of shame on their heads.

676
00:45:47,900 --> 00:45:52,340
Don't let evil conquer you, but conquer evil by doing good.

677
00:45:53,260 --> 00:46:03,560
Father, may this passage be true of our church as we take seriously the invitation to go deeper into the gospel moment by moment and day by day.

678
00:46:03,560 --> 00:46:07,760
May we make room for you to do whatever you want to do in our lives.

679
00:46:09,520 --> 00:46:14,260
May we become a temple of the Holy Spirit.

680
00:46:14,260 --> 00:46:22,080
In this pocket of our little town in Winchester, may the light of Jesus shine outside of these walls because we take your word seriously.

681
00:46:23,360 --> 00:46:28,000
Because we welcome the invitation to step into our calling.

682
00:46:28,000 --> 00:46:30,840
We love you so much, Jesus.

683
00:46:30,840 --> 00:46:32,840
It's in your name we pray.

684
00:46:32,840 --> 00:46:33,700
Amen.

685
00:46:33,700 --> 00:46:36,180
Go in peace, church.

686
00:46:36,180 --> 00:46:40,340
Please, I'd love for those of you that are new, want to get connected to stay for some pizza.

687
00:46:40,340 --> 00:46:42,760
15 minutes in the kids' room.

688
00:46:42,760 --> 00:46:44,740
Let's give them time to get out and we'll be there.

689
00:46:53,360 --> 00:46:55,180
Let's give them time to get connected to stay for some pizza.

690
00:46:55,180 --> 00:46:56,300
Let's give them time to get connected to stay for some pizza.

691
00:46:56,300 --> 00:46:57,240
Let's give them time to stay for some pizza.

692
00:46:57,240 --> 00:46:58,300
